@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}
<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>

<p>
    OneClickSocialMedia (“we”, “us”) helps you publish content to multiple social media platforms from one place.
    This Privacy Policy explains what data we collect, why we collect it, and how we protect it.
</p>

<h2>What we collect</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Connected social accounts:</strong> When you connect a social media platform, we receive authorization data (e.g., OAuth tokens) so we can post on your behalf.</li>
    <li><strong>Content you submit:</strong> Posts you write, images/videos you upload, and the platforms you select.</li>
    <li><strong>Usage data:</strong> Basic analytics such as pages visited, feature usage, device/browser info, and diagnostic logs to improve reliability.</li>
</ul>

<h2>How we use your information</h2>
<ul>
    <li>To connect your chosen social media accounts and publish your posts as requested.</li>
    <li>To show you posting status (success/failure) and any error messages returned by platforms.</li>
    <li>To maintain, troubleshoot, and improve performance and security.</li>
    <li>To communicate important service updates (if you provide contact details).</li>
</ul>

<h2>Connected social platforms</h2>
<p>
    When you connect a platform, you grant us permission to perform actions you approve (such as creating posts).
    Each platform has its own privacy policy and rules. We recommend reviewing them.
</p>

<h2>How we store and protect tokens</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Access tokens are treated as sensitive data.</li>
    <li>We store tokens securely and use them only to perform actions you request.</li>
    <li>We use industry-standard security measures such as encryption in transit (HTTPS) and access controls.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Data retention</h2>
<p>
    We keep your data only as long as needed to provide the service. You can disconnect social accounts at any time.
    If you delete your account, we will delete or anonymize data where feasible, unless we must keep it for legal or security reasons.
</p>

<h2>Sharing your information</h2>
<p>
    We do not sell your personal data. We only share information:
</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>With social media platforms:</strong> to publish content you request.</li>
    <li><strong>With service providers:</strong> hosting, logging, or monitoring providers that help us run the app (under appropriate safeguards).</li>
    <li><strong>For legal reasons:</strong> if required by law or to protect our rights and users.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Your choices</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Disconnect a social account at any time (this stops future posting to that platform).</li>
    <li>Request deletion of your account and associated data where applicable.</li>
    <li>Update your posting preferences and stored content within the app.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Cookies</h2>
<p>
    We may use essential cookies for sign-in and security, and optional cookies/analytics to understand how the app is used.
    You can control cookies through your browser settings.
</p>

<h2>Children’s privacy</h2>
<p>
    OneClickSocialMedia is not intended for children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal data from children.
</p>

<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. If we make significant changes, we will post the updated policy here.
</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>
    If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, contact us at:
    <br />
    <strong>Email:</strong> support@oneclicksocialmedia.example
</p>
